_with_caveats","summary":"Constant g is the right reading of a half-second drop. The uncertainty budget is dominated by the sheet's scale, as it should be.","issues":[{"id":"R1-1","severity":"minor","claim":"g is quoted to a precision finer than the scale uncertainty alone.","evidence":"Scale uncertainty is 0.35% and the plane offset 0.25%.","requested_action":"add_caveat","detail":"Keep the calibration terms in the headline interval."}],"response_md":"The headline interval already includes the calibration terms; the budget table lists them."}]},"ghosts":[{"id":"gh-fall-1","version":1,"trial_id":"fall-t2","model_id":"FF0","model_name":"FF0: Constant gravity","video_url":"/mock/drop-ghost.mp4","slow_video_url":"/mock/drop-ghost-slow.mp4","track_url":"mock:ghost/ex-free-fall/v1","poster_url":"/mock/drop-poster.jpg","divergence_onset_s":null,"max_error_mm":4.405795,"threshold_mm":10,"predicted_ahead_s":0.2291667,"revision":null}],"whatif":{"system":"free_fall","model_ref":"FF0","params":{"g":9.753782},"fixed":{},"initial":{"y0":1.200299,"v0":-0.005326411},"measured_range":{"height_m":[1.1,1.3]},"object":{"name":"Steel ball","radius_m":0.02,"mass_kg":0.067},"still_url":"/mock/drop-still.jpg","sim_supported":true,"anchor_m":[0,0]},"export_formats":[],"quality_flags":[],"job":null,"error":null,"last_seq":16},"events":[{"id":1,"experiment_id":"ex-free-fall","seq":1,"ts":"2026-10-27T16:40:03.000Z","phase":"normalize","actor":"system","kind":"observation","title":"Clip normalized","body_md":"Read **116 frames** at 240 fps (constant frame rate). Time factor 1, jitter 0.4%. Every frame has a real timestamp.","data":{"timing":{"classification":"cfr","detected_fps":240,"declared_mode":"slow_mo","declared_fps":240,"time_factor":1,"jitter_pct":0.4,"warnings":[]}},"attachments":[],"refs":[]},{"id":2,"experiment_id":"ex-free-fall","seq":2,"ts":"2026-10-27T16:40:07.000Z","phase":"watch","actor":"wonder","kind":"observation","title":"Wonder watched the clip","body_md":"A steel ball is released from rest beside a wall with an A4 sheet on it, and falls about 1.2 m.","data":{"tracked_objects":[{"key":"ball","sam_prompt":"steel ball","role":"moving_body","why":"The falling object."}],"quality_issues":[]},"attachments":[],"refs":[]},{"id":3,"experiment_id":"ex-free-fall","seq":3,"ts":"2026-10-27T16:40:12.000Z","phase":"track","actor":"sam","kind":"observation","title":"SAM 3.1 tracked 1 object","body_md":"- \"steel ball\" (moving_body): The falling object.","data":{},"attachments":[],"refs":[]},{"id":4,"experiment_id":"ex-free-fall","seq":4,"ts":"2026-10-27T16:40:18.000Z","phase":"calibrate","actor":"harness","kind":"observation","title":"Scale and timing calibrated","body_md":"The A4 sheet gives **2.86 mm per pixel** with 0.35% uncertainty. Plane offset 2.5 cm; camera moved 0.3 px over the clip.","data":{"calibration":{"paper":"a4","mm_per_px":2.86,"sigma_scale_rel":0.0035,"plane_offset_cm":2.5,"gravity_source":"data","ramp_angle_deg":null,"camera_motion_px":0.3}},"attachments":[],"refs":[]},{"id":5,"experiment_id":"ex-free-fall","seq":5,"ts":"2026-10-27T16:40:20.000Z","phase":"hypothesize","actor":"wonder","kind":"hypothesis","title":"Hypothesis FF0: Constant gravity","body_md":"Gravity alone: a constant downward acceleration g, with no air.\n\n$$\\ddot y=-g$$\n\n**Refuted if:** y(t) is an exact parabola. Systematic curvature left in the residuals, growing with speed, refutes it.","data":{"model_id":"FF0","prior_rank":1},"attachments":[],"refs":[]},{"id":6,"experiment_id":"ex-free-fall","seq":6,"ts":"2026-10-27T16:40:23.000Z","phase":"hypothesize","actor":"wonder","kind":"hypothesis","title":"Hypothesis FF1: Linear drag","body_md":"Gravity plus air drag proportional to speed.\n\n$$\\ddot y=-g-\\frac{b}{m}\\,\\dot y$$\n\n**Refuted if:** The acceleration shrinks as the ball speeds up. If b/m fits to zero, drag is not needed.","data":{"model_id":"FF1","prior_rank":2},"attachments":[],"refs":[]},{"id":7,"experiment_id":"ex-free-fall","seq":7,"ts":"2026-10-27T16:40:27.000Z","phase":"hypothesize","actor":"wonder","kind":"hypothesis","title":"Hypothesis FF2: Quadratic drag","body_md":"Gravity plus quadratic air drag, the usual law for a ball moving through air at speed.\n\n$$\\ddot y=-g-\\frac{k}{m}\\,|\\dot y|\\,\\dot y$$\n\n**Refuted if:** Drag matters only near the end of the fall, where the speed is highest.","data":{"model_id":"FF2","prior_rank":3},"attachments":[],"refs":[]},{"id":8,"experiment_id":"ex-free-fall","seq":8,"ts":"2026-10-27T16:40:32.000Z","phase":"hypothesize","actor":"wonder","kind":"prediction","title":"Prediction made before any fit: Constant gravity","body_md":"Before looking at a single fit, I expect **Constant gravity**. I will count it refuted if this happens: y(t) is an exact parabola. Systematic curvature left in the residuals, growing with speed, refutes it.\n\nThe harness scores every model on the last 35% of the motion, which I never see.","data":{"model_id":"FF0","pinned":"prediction"},"attachments":[],"refs":[]},{"id":9,"experiment_id":"ex-free-fall","seq":9,"ts":"2026-10-27T16:40:38.000Z","phase":"fit","actor":"harness","kind":"fit","title":"Fit FF0: Constant gravity","body_md":"Fitted on the first 65% of the motion, then forecast the rest.\n\n- y₀: **1.201** (1.2 to 1.2) m\n- v₀: **-0.01202** (-0.0414 to 0.0174) m/s\n- g: **9.712** (9.41 to 10) m/s²\n\nTraining RMSE **0.00157 m**. Held-out RMSE **0.00186 m** (0.00131 to 0.00225). Lowest on 1 of 3 splits.","data":{"model_id":"FF0","split":0.65,"rerunnable":true,"fit":[{"name":"y0","label":"y₀","value":1.200628,"ci_low":1.197454,"ci_high":1.203802,"unit":"m","kind":"initial_condition"},{"name":"v0","label":"v₀","value":-0.01202092,"ci_low":-0.04142092,"ci_high":0.01737908,"unit":"m/s","kind":"initial_condition"},{"name":"g","label":"g","value":9.711587,"ci_low":9.412996,"ci_high":10.01018,"unit":"m/s²","kind":"physical"}],"diagnostics":{"reduced_chi2":1.137516,"lag1_autocorr":-0.05582766,"durbin_watson":2.067508,"runs_p":0.9675653,"systematic_residual":false}},"attachments":[],"refs":[]},{"id":10,"experiment_id":"ex-free-fall","seq":10,"ts":"2026-10-27T16:40:40.000Z","phase":"fit","actor":"harness","kind":"fit","title":"Fit FF1: Linear drag","body_md":"Fitted on the first 65% of the motion, then forecast the rest.\n\n- y₀: **1.2** (1.2 to 1.2) m\n- v₀: **-0.002664** (-0.0321 to 0.0267) m/s\n- g: **9.865** (8.07 to 11.7) m/s²\n- b/m (linear drag rate): **0.1017** (0.0419 to 0.161) 1/s\n\nTraining RMSE **0.00156 m**. Held-out RMSE **0.0039 m** (0.00219 to 0.00495). Lowest on 2 of 3 splits.","data":{"model_id":"FF1","split":0.65,"rerunnable":true,"fit":[{"name":"y0","label":"y₀","value":1.200396,"ci_low":1.196231,"ci_high":1.204561,"unit":"m","kind":"initial_condition"},{"name":"v0","label":"v₀","value":-0.002664224,"ci_low":-0.03206422,"ci_high":0.02673578,"unit":"m/s","kind":"initial_condition"},{"name":"g","label":"g","value":9.865071,"ci_low":8.071526,"ci_high":11.65862,"unit":"m/s²","kind":"physical"},{"name":"b_over_m","label":"b/m (linear drag rate)","value":0.1016513,"ci_low":0.04188034,"ci_high":0.1614223,"unit":"1/s","kind":"physical"}],"diagnostics":{"reduced_chi2":1.149318,"lag1_autocorr":-0.06434283,"durbin_watson":2.076468,"runs_p":0.6970681,"systematic_residual":false}},"attachments":[],"refs":[]},{"id":11,"experiment_id":"ex-free-fall","seq":11,"ts":"2026-10-27T16:40:43.000Z","phase":"fit","actor":"harness","kind":"fit","title":"Fit FF2: Quadratic drag","body_md":"Fitted on the first 65% of the motion, then forecast the rest.\n\n- y₀: **1.201** (0.495 to 1.91) m\n- v₀: **-0.01202** (-0.0191 to -0.00495) m/s\n- g: **9.712** (5 to 15.4) m/s²\n- k/m (quadratic drag): **0.02619** (0.0108 to 0.0416) 1/m\n\nTraining RMSE **0.00157 m**. Held-out RMSE **0.00186 m** (0.00131 to 0.00225). Lowest on 0 of 3 splits.","data":{"model_id":"FF2","split":0.65,"rerunnable":true,"fit":[{"name":"y0","label":"y₀","value":1.200628,"ci_low":0.4946587,"ci_high":1.906597,"unit":"m","kind":"initial_conditio